let w = dataset(wages).where(year == 2019)
w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ + exper + I(exper^2))
---- exit code 1
error[Z0103]: no function is called `I`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:34
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ + exper + I(exper^2))
  |                                  ^ not a function of Zeff
  |
  = help: arithmetic in a formula is worked out before fitting, so `I()` is not needed: write `exper^2`

